WEBVTT

00:15:28.206 --> 00:15:30.213
And once you allow fear
to just be present,

00:15:30.237 --> 00:15:33.825
it seems to quiet down and go to sleep,
and then you can go about your work.

00:15:33.849 --> 00:15:35.730
But it's never out of the picture,

00:15:35.754 --> 00:15:38.913
and I don't waste my energy
trying to kick it out of the picture,

00:15:38.937 --> 00:15:42.886
because that feels to me like just
a colossal, exhausting waste of energy,

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:47.010
whereas a radical, inclusive
self-acceptance seems to be a way

00:15:47.034 --> 00:15:48.577
to be able to create a lot more.

00:15:48.601 --> 00:15:50.061
CA: Yeah. No, that's powerful.

00:15:50.085 --> 00:15:53.207
A lot of people are frightened
of giving a TED Talk,

00:15:53.231 --> 00:15:56.320
and one of the things we try and say is,

00:15:56.344 --> 00:15:58.879
if you can embrace that fear,
make it your friend,

00:15:58.903 --> 00:16:03.399
it actually can be the motivation
that helps you make a much better talk.